        "attempt": 1,
        "status": "OK",
        "duration_seconds": 49.181,
        "asr_text": "But the announcement was limited. It did not name the system, explain its exact attack method, or identify a target. So the confirmed news is that the United States has publicly acknowledged deploying weapons in orbit. It is not confirmation that those weapons have attacked a satellite. Other claims need a different label. A 2025 U.S. intelligence assessment said Russia was developing a satellite with a nuclear weapon for anti-satellite use, but the assessment did not say that the satellite had been launched, placed in orbit, or used. That difference matters. Announced, being developed, tested, and deployed are not the same thing.",
